messages:
jordan: Seeing a spike in onboarding tickets: users confused by import styles in the JS SDK. Quickstart only shows one pattern and it fails in a few setups.
priya: Common failures: "named export not found" when using `import { InferenceClient } ...` (package published with default-only), or `undefined` after `const x = require('@redwood/inference')` when consumers expect named fields. Also TS without esModuleInterop trips people.
evan: We should add a tiny cheatsheet and 4 example apps (cjs / esm / ts / edge). Copy/paste fixes most first-time errors.
priya: Proposed README snippets (short):
```
// Node CommonJS (package.json without "type": "module")
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood.InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// Node ESM default import ("type": "module" or .mjs)
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood.InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// ESM named import (edge runtimes / strict ESM)
import { InferenceClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const client2 = new InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// TypeScript (if you don't enable esModuleInterop)
import Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const clientTs = new (Redwood as any).InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
```
priya: Add short notes: require() may return a namespace with a `.default` if the package was published with an ESM default export; `import { Named }` fails when package only exports default; TS users without `esModuleInterop` should see tsconfig suggestion.
evan: Edge reminder: Vercel/Cloudflare runtime is ESM-only. Show edge example using named import:
```
import { InferenceClient } from '@redwood/inference';
export default async function handler(req) {
  const c = new InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
  const out = await c.generate({ prompt: 'hello' });
  return new Response(JSON.stringify(out));
}
```
build-eng: Ops notes: ensure package.json contains both `main` (CJS) and `module` (ESM) keys, `types` pointing at .d.ts, and CI publishes both dist/cjs and dist/esm. Filing INF-342 to normalize build outputs and add e2e tests that run example apps.
docs-bot: Draft PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/538 — adds "JS SDK: CJS / ESM / TS / Edge" section and links to examples.
jordan: Short-term plan: 1) update quickstart README with cheatsheet + link to examples, 2) add examples/js/{cjs,esm,ts,edge}, 3) follow up on INF-342. Also update onboarding checklist so support can point users immediately.
priya: I'll scaffold the examples and add minimal run instructions + a tsconfig snippet suggestion: ```{ "compilerOptions": { "esModuleInterop": true, "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true } }```
jordan: Great — once the docs PR lands we'll push the onboarding micro-update. Thanks all, closing thread.
